{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2968","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2968","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2968\",\"parent_revision\":\"c2b49103e4be2b0ea810bb8d1576dfabd10a19b341a27ad4bb4b78499310390a\",\"root_revision\":\"c2b49103e4be2b0ea810bb8d1576dfabd10a19b341a27ad4bb4b78499310390a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-18\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDiscovered via a hypothesis property test written while reworking #2956's fix (PR #2964), related to #2966 (Unicode title-casing round trip) but a distinct root cause.\\n\\nrendering.heading_to_unknown_key() encodes a section display name into a storage key by lowercasing and replacing every space with an underscore (\\\"Impact Radius\\\" -> \\\"unknown__impact_radius\\\"). This encoding is ambiguous/lossy for any display name that itself contains a literal underscore, or that (after ATX-heading whitespace normalization on re-parse) collapses to something indistinguishable from an underscore-only string.\\n\\nConcrete falsifying example: section_name = \\\"_\\\" (a single underscore).\\n- heading_to_unknown_key(\\\"_\\\") -> key = \\\"unknown___\\\" (three underscores: the \\\"unknown__\\\" prefix plus the literal \\\"_\\\").\\n- unknown_key_to_heading(\\\"unknown___\\\") -> strips the \\\"unknown__\\\" prefix, leaving \\\"_\\\" -> replace(\\\"_\\\", \\\" \\\") -> \\\" \\\" (a single space) -> .title() -> \\\" \\\" (unchanged). The heading text is now a single space.\\n- Rendered as \\\"##  \\\" (two spaces after the ATX marker). On re-parse, the ATX heading regex's \\\\s+ consumes all the whitespace, leaving an EMPTY heading name.\\n- Re-normalizing \\\"\\\" produces key \\\"unknown__\\\" (only the prefix, two underscores) -- different from the original \\\"unknown___\\\".\\n\\nImpact: narrow -- only affects section names that are literal underscores/whitespace-only after stripping, an unrealistic input for a human/agent-authored display name (no one names a section \\\"_\\\"). Confirmed distinct from #2966 (that one is a Unicode str.title() casing quirk; this one is the underscore-as-space-separator encoding itself being non-invertible for names containing literal underscores).\\n\\n**Research first**: a full fix likely requires either escaping literal underscores in the source name before substituting for spaces (so the two are distinguishable on the reverse transform), or storing the original display name verbatim instead of round-tripping it through a lossy encode/decode pair -- the same design question raised in #2966. Consider resolving both together.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **unknown-section key encoding conflates literal underscores in a section name with space-substitution underscores** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input, found via hypothesis property test written for #2956\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a831b4a95c1f2a309430e69f8e60acea828264f9b20678c3a4daafd680e4cd9d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPUW43w\"}"}